            <ArticleTitle>Percutaneous transcatheter repair of a coronary aneurysm using a composite autologous cephalic vein-coated Palmaz-Schatz biliary stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>990-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a novel percutaneous transcatheter technique using an autologous vein graft-coated Palmaz-Schatz stent for the treatment of a coronary aneurysm. This technique avoids the procedural risks that are currently associated with surgical repair with revascularization or spring coil embolization in the treatment of coronary aneurysm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
